{% set local_problem %}
<p>Priceville's tree coverage means consistent gutter maintenance for most homeowners. Established neighborhoods have mature trees that drop massive amounts of leaves every fall. Properties along the river roads collect debris year-round from the surrounding pine and hardwood forests.</p>

<p>When gutters clog, the problems start quickly. Overflowing water runs down your siding, pools around your foundation, and eventually finds its way into places it shouldn't be. Morgan County's clay soil means that pooled water often stays pooled, creating conditions for foundation damage and basement moisture.</p>

<p>Many Priceville homeowners try to handle gutter cleaning themselves, but it's time-consuming and potentially dangerous work. Climbing ladders, reaching across rooflines, dealing with decomposed debris — it's not a pleasant way to spend a Saturday. And for homes with steep roofs or multiple stories, DIY cleaning can be genuinely risky.</p>

<p>That's where we come in. We're just 8 miles away in Hartselle, which means we can respond quickly and fit Priceville into our regular service routes easily. Fast, thorough, and right in your neighborhood.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our gutter cleaning service is comprehensive. We start by hand-removing all debris from inside your gutters — leaves, pine needles, roof grit, decomposed organic matter, and anything else that's accumulated. We don't just blow debris onto your lawn or push it toward the downspouts.</p>

<p>Next, we flush all downspouts with water to ensure they're clear and flowing properly. Downspout clogs are a common problem that many homeowners miss — debris backs up in the downspout, and the gutter overflows even though it looks clean from above.</p>

<p>Finally, we inspect your entire gutter system: hangers, seams, slope, and the fascia boards behind. We'll flag developing problems before they become expensive repairs. When we're done, we clean up all debris from your landscaping.</p>
{% endset %}

